---
import PageLayout from "blume/components/layout/PageLayout.astro";
import data from "blume:data";
const { config } = data;
const sections = [["01", "The bridge", "bridge"], ["02", "Your hardware", "hardware"], ["03", "Pair & approve", "pairing"], ["04", "Start locally", "setup"], ["05", "Project status", "status"]];
---
<PageLayout site={{ title: config.title, description: config.description }} logo={config.logo} banner={config.banner} navigation={data.navigation} favicon={config.favicon} fontCssVars={data.fontCssVars} themeMode={config.theme.mode} searchEnabled={config.search.enabled} siteUrl={config.site} ogEnabled={config.og.enabled} page={{ title: "openlaunch — Your agents. Your devices. Your permission.", description: config.description }}>
  <div class="home">
    <aside class="rail" aria-label="Page navigation">
      <p class="rail-label">FROM PROMPT TO DEVICE</p>
      <nav>{sections.map(([n, label, id]) => <a href={`#${id}`}><span>{n}</span>{label}</a>)}</nav>
      <div class="rail-bottom"><span class="tiny-dot"></span> Built in the open<p>Small capabilities.<br />Explicit permission.</p><a href="https://github.com/pkyanam/openlaunch">Explore the source ↗</a></div>
    </aside>
    <article>
      <section class="hero">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="tiny-dot"></span> PROVIDER-NEUTRAL DEVICE BRIDGE</p>
        <h1>Your agents.<br />Your devices.<br /><em>Your permission.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">Give your agent a small, approved way to interact with the physical world. Pair a device, choose its capabilities, and keep control of every grant.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="primary" href="/docs/setup">Start locally <span>↗</span></a><a class="secondary" href="/docs">Read the docs <span>→</span></a></div>
        <p class="hero-note">Developer alpha. Local software tested; real hardware acceptance pending.</p>
        <figure class="flow" aria-label="Illustration of an agent request passing through owner approval to a device">
          <div class="flow-top"><span>ONE BOUNDED REQUEST</span><span>Illustration · no live device</span></div>
          <div class="flow-nodes"><div><span class="node-symbol">⌘</span><strong>Your agent</strong><small>Requests a capability</small></div><span class="arrow">→</span><div class="gate"><span class="node-symbol">✓</span><strong>openlaunch</strong><small>Checks your grant + TTL</small></div><span class="arrow">→</span><div><span class="node-symbol">▦</span><strong>Your device</strong><small>Executes & reports</small></div></div>
          <div class="flow-bottom"><code>show_text("hello")</code><span>queued → received → completed</span></div>
        </figure>
      </section>
      <section id="bridge">
        <p class="section-index">01 / THE BRIDGE</p><h2>A little access goes a long way.</h2>
        <p class="intro">Start with a health check, a built-in LED, or a short message on a matrix. The bridge translates typed agent requests into bounded device actions.</p>
        <div class="principles"><div><span>↔</span><h3>Bring your agent</h3><p>A shared MCP interface for local Codex today. Hosted ChatGPT onboarding and other integrations are planned.</p></div><div><span>⊞</span><h3>Keep it modular</h3><p>Protocol, authorization, transports and hardware adapters stay independent. Provider credentials stay off firmware.</p></div><div><span>⌁</span><h3>Keep your say</h3><p>You approve capabilities per agent and device, with a bounded lifetime. Pairing alone grants no agent access.</p></div></div>
        <a class="text-link" href="/docs/architecture">Inside the architecture →</a>
      </section>
      <section id="hardware">
        <p class="section-index">02 / YOUR HARDWARE</p><h2>Two boards. A clear starting point.</h2><p class="intro">Software targets with deliberately small capability sets. Physical operation still needs acceptance testing.</p>
        <div class="hardware-grid"><a class="hardware-card" href="/docs/uno-r4"><div class="board-art uno" aria-hidden="true"><span class="port"></span><span class="chip"></span><span class="matrix">••••••<br />••••••<br />••••••<br />••••••</span><span class="board-label">R4 / WiFi</span><span class="pins"></span></div><div class="card-copy"><span class="tag">FIRMWARE COMPILES</span><h3>Arduino Uno R4 WiFi</h3><p>Health, built-in LED and ASCII matrix text. Isolated stock and repaired console-mux build profiles.</p><span class="text-link">Board setup →</span></div></a><a class="hardware-card" href="/docs/pi"><div class="board-art pi" aria-hidden="true"><span class="port"></span><span class="chip"></span><span class="sockets"></span><span class="board-label">Pi 4 / Model B</span><span class="pins"></span></div><div class="card-copy"><span class="tag">REAL RUNTIME: HEALTH ONLY</span><h3>Raspberry Pi 4 Model B</h3><p>4GB or 8GB. A Go agent for Linux ARM64 or ARMv7. GPIO and display adapters remain future work.</p><span class="text-link">Pi setup →</span></div></a></div>
      </section>
      <section id="pairing">
        <p class="section-index">03 / PAIR & APPROVE</p><h2>Connected doesn't mean authorized.</h2><p class="intro">Device enrollment and agent permissions are two separate decisions you make.</p>
        <ol class="steps"><li><span>1</span><div><h3>Create an enrollment</h3><p>Choose the board kind in your local owner console. Its single-use enrollment expires after 10 minutes.</p></div><small>OWNER</small></li><li><span>2</span><div><h3>Pair the device</h3><p>The device exchanges the enrollment for its own credential. Use USB provisioning for R4 or the Go agent for Pi.</p></div><small>DEVICE</small></li><li><span>3</span><div><h3>Approve a capability</h3><p>Choose the agent, device, capability and grant lifetime. You can revoke access later.</p></div><small>OWNER</small></li><li><span>4</span><div><h3>Inspect the outcome</h3><p>Commands have a TTL and distinct queued, received and terminal states. Current delivery polls every 10 seconds.</p></div><small>BRIDGE</small></li></ol>
        <p class="footnote">A queued request is not a successful physical action. Disconnects can leave an uncertain outcome.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/pairing">Read pairing & permission rules →</a>
      </section>
      <section id="setup" class="setup-section">
        <p class="section-index">04 / START LOCALLY</p><h2>From source to your workbench.</h2><p class="intro">Run the local bridge and React console on your machine. Start with the simulated client, then follow the hardware acceptance guides.</p>
        <div class="terminal"><div><span>LOCAL DEVELOPMENT</span><span>macOS / Node 24+</span></div><pre><code>git clone https://github.com/pkyanam/openlaunch.git
cd openlaunch
npm ci
npm run check
npm run build</code></pre></div><p class="footnote">Go and Arduino prerequisites, disposable tokens and HTTPS board setup are covered in the guide. The commands above build software; they don't flash a board.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="primary" href="/docs/setup">Follow the setup guide <span>→</span></a><a class="secondary" href="https://github.com/pkyanam/openlaunch">View on GitHub <span>↗</span></a></div>
      </section>
      <section id="status">
        <p class="section-index">05 / PROJECT STATUS</p><h2>Built in the open. Still an alpha.</h2><p class="intro">The foundations work locally. Hosted onboarding and real device verification are the next gates.</p>
        <div class="status-grid"><div><span class="tag">IMPLEMENTED LOCALLY</span><h3>The working foundation</h3><p>SQLite bridge, shared permission engine, command lifecycle, React owner console, MCP tools and simulated end-to-end tests.</p></div><div><span class="tag pending">PENDING ACCEPTANCE</span><h3>Before public controls</h3><p>Hosted login, OAuth consent and refresh, secure dashboard sessions, production deployment and physical Pi/R4 testing.</p></div></div><a class="text-link" href="/docs/status">See limitations & next steps →</a>
      </section>
      <footer class="home-footer"><strong>openlaunch</strong><span>Your hardware. On your terms.</span><a href="/docs">Documentation ↗</a></footer>
    </article>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
<style is:global>
.home{--ink:#202622;--muted:#626b65;--line:#dfe5df;--paper:#fafbf8;--accent:#166453;color:var(--ink);background:var(--paper);display:grid;grid-template-columns:210px minmax(0,1fr);max-width:1440px;margin:auto;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif}.home *{box-sizing:border-box}.home a{text-decoration:none;color:inherit}.home a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #399782;outline-offset:5px}.rail{border-right:1px solid var(--line);padding:52px 26px;position:sticky;top:100px;align-self:start;height:calc(100vh - 100px);display:flex;flex-direction:column}.rail-label,.eyebrow,.section-index,.tag,.flow-top,.flow-bottom,.terminal>div,.rail nav span{font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Consolas,monospace}.rail-label{font-size:9px;letter-spacing:1px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.8}.rail nav{display:grid;gap:20px;margin-top:32px;font-size:12px}.rail nav a:hover,.text-link:hover,.secondary:hover{color:var(--accent)}.rail nav span{color:var(--muted);font-size:10px;margin-right:14px}.rail-bottom{margin-top:auto;font-size:11px}.rail-bottom p{color:var(--muted);line-height:1.8;margin:15px 0}.tiny-dot{width:7px;height:7px;background:#287960;border-radius:50%;display:inline-block;margin-right:8px}.home article{min-width:0;padding:0 64px}.home section{padding:72px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);scroll-margin-top:120px}.home .hero{padding-top:66px}.eyebrow,.section-index{font-size:10px;letter-spacing:1.5px;color:var(--accent);margin:0 0 26px}.home h1{font-size:clamp(52px,5.6vw,80px);letter-spacing:-4px;line-height:1.04;font-weight:500;margin:0 0 30px}.home h1 em{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;color:var(--accent);letter-spacing:-3px}.lede{font-size:19px;line-height:1.65;max-width:570px;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 30px}.actions{display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap}.primary,.secondary{padding:13px 19px;border-radius:5px;font-size:13px;display:inline-flex;gap:28px;align-items:center}.home .primary{background:var(--ink);color:#fff}.primary:hover{background:var(--accent)}.secondary{border:1px solid var(--line)}.hero-note,.footnote{font-size:12px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted);margin:20px 0}.flow{margin:48px 0 0;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:9px;background:#fff;overflow:hidden}.flow-top,.flow-bottom{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:15px;padding:15px 22px;font-size:9px;color:var(--muted)}.flow-top{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);letter-spacing:.7px}.flow-nodes{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 30px 1.3fr 30px 1fr;align-items:center;padding:28px 24px}.flow-nodes>div{text-align:center;padding:18px 5px}.flow strong,.flow small{display:block}.flow strong{font-size:13px;margin:10px 0 7px}.flow small{font-size:10px;color:var(--muted)}.node-symbol{font-size:25px}.gate{border:1px solid #bbd4c9;background:#edf4ef;border-radius:8px;color:var(--accent)}.arrow{text-align:center;color:#8e9c92}.flow-bottom{border-top:1px solid var(--line);background:#f6f8f4;font-size:10px}.home h2{font-size:32px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-1px;margin:0 0 18px}.intro{max-width:650px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 28px}.home h3{font-size:16px;font-weight:500;margin:15px 0 10px}.principles{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:7px;margin:30px 0 24px}.principles>div{padding:25px 20px}.principles>div+div{border-left:1px solid var(--line)}.principles>div>span{font-size:23px;color:var(--accent)}.principles p,.card-copy p,.status-grid p{font-size:13px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--muted);margin:0}.text-link{font-size:12px;color:var(--accent)!important;display:inline-block;margin-top:8px}.hardware-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.hardware-card{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:7px;overflow:hidden;transition:transform .2s,border-color .2s}.hardware-card:hover{transform:translateY(-3px);border-color:#90b5a5}.card-copy{padding:24px}.card-copy h3{font-size:20px;letter-spacing:-.4px}.card-copy .text-link{margin-top:20px}.board-art{position:relative;height:190px;background-color:#f0f3ed;background-image:radial-gradient(#d3dacf 1px,transparent 1px);background-size:14px 14px;overflow:hidden}.board-art:before{content:'';position:absolute;background:#40736c;width:190px;height:112px;left:50%;top:50%;transform:translate(-50%,-50%) rotate(-7deg);border-radius:8px;box-shadow:0 14px 22px #14282025;border:3px solid #568b81}.board-art.pi:before{background:#47794a;border-color:#679266;transform:translate(-50%,-50%) rotate(7deg)}.board-art .chip{position:absolute;left:42%;top:38%;width:42px;height:42px;background:#283a34;border:4px solid #90a597}.board-art .port{position:absolute;left:calc(50% - 108px);top:60px;width:33px;height:36px;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#b1b7af,#e2e4dc);border:1px solid #a5aea2;transform:rotate(-7deg)}.matrix{position:absolute;left:55%;top:51px;color:#f4ba80;font:bold 13px/12px monospace;letter-spacing:3px;transform:rotate(-7deg);background:#273c34;padding:6px}.board-label{position:absolute;left:calc(50% - 61px);top:135px;font:9px monospace;color:#fff;transform:rotate(-7deg)}.pins{position:absolute;left:calc(50% - 64px);top:38px;width:140px;height:9px;background:repeating-linear-gradient(90deg,#293b30 0 4px,#bcbba1 4px 7px);transform:rotate(-7deg)}.pi .pins{transform:rotate(7deg);top:40px}.pi .board-label{transform:rotate(7deg);top:128px}.pi .sockets{position:absolute;left:calc(50% + 53px);top:64px;width:48px;height:60px;background:repeating-linear-gradient(#c4cdc0 0 26px,#465640 26px 30px);transform:rotate(7deg);border:2px solid #a3b59d}.tag{font-size:8px;letter-spacing:1px;color:var(--accent)}.steps{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:28px 0}.steps li{display:flex;gap:20px;align-items:flex-start;padding:25px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.steps li>span{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:50%;width:30px;height:30px;flex-shrink:0;display:grid;place-items:center;font:12px monospace}.steps li>div{flex:1}.steps h3{margin:2px 0 8px}.steps p{font-size:13px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--muted);max-width:530px;margin:0}.steps small{font:9px monospace;letter-spacing:.7px;color:var(--muted);padding-top:8px}.terminal{background:#202b25;color:#f5f8f0;border-radius:7px;overflow:hidden}.terminal>div{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;padding:16px 22px;border-bottom:1px solid #ffffff20;font-size:9px;color:#b3c6b8;letter-spacing:.6px}.terminal pre{padding:24px;margin:0;font-size:12px;line-height:2;overflow-x:auto}.status-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:28px;margin:32px 0 25px}.status-grid>div{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:25px}.pending{color:#8b611c}.home-footer{padding:30px 0 45px;display:flex;gap:20px;font-size:11px;align-items:center}.home-footer strong{font-size:15px}.home-footer span{color:var(--muted);flex:1}.home-footer a{color:var(--accent)}
:root[data-theme='dark'] .home,:root.dark .home{--ink:#e8eee8;--muted:#a5b2a8;--line:#35453a;--paper:#18211b;--accent:#8bccb0}.dark .flow,[data-theme='dark'] .flow{background:#202d24}.dark .gate,[data-theme='dark'] .gate{background:#263c30;border-color:#526d59}.dark .flow-bottom,[data-theme='dark'] .flow-bottom{background:#202d24}.dark .primary,[data-theme='dark'] .primary{color:#18211b}
@media(min-width:1500px){.home article{padding:0 85px}}@media(max-width:1000px){.home{grid-template-columns:160px 1fr}.home article{padding:0 32px}.rail{padding:40px 16px}.rail-label{font-size:8px}.rail nav{font-size:11px}.home h1{font-size:60px}.principles{grid-template-columns:1fr}.principles>div+div{border-left:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.flow-nodes{padding:20px 10px}.flow-bottom{font-size:9px}.board-art:before{width:170px}.hardware-grid{gap:14px}}
@media(max-width:700px){.home{display:block}.rail{display:none}.home article{padding:0 23px}.home section{padding:48px 0}.home .hero{padding-top:42px}.home h1{font-size:53px;letter-spacing:-2.7px}.home h1 em{letter-spacing:-2px}.lede{font-size:16px}.home h2{font-size:28px}.intro{font-size:14px}.eyebrow{font-size:8px;letter-spacing:1px}.flow{margin-top:32px}.flow-top{padding:13px;font-size:7px;letter-spacing:0}.flow-nodes{grid-template-columns:1fr 14px 1.2fr 14px 1fr;padding:18px 8px}.flow strong{font-size:11px}.flow small{font-size:8px;line-height:1.5}.flow-bottom{flex-direction:column;gap:8px;padding:13px}.hardware-grid,.status-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.board-art{height:180px}.steps{margin-bottom:15px}.steps li{gap:12px}.steps small{font-size:7px}.terminal>div{font-size:7px;padding:14px}.terminal pre{padding:18px;font-size:10px}.hero-note,.footnote{font-size:11px}.home-footer{flex-wrap:wrap}.home-footer span{flex-basis:60%}.secondary,.primary{font-size:12px;padding:12px 16px}}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.hardware-card{transition:none}}
</style>
